### X2b diff read: PASS
- The guards diff adds TRY_EXCEPTIONS (3 entries, all `l2-w01-story-page-a-nut`: line +1 PM 09:17 ICT,
  color +1 and line +1 PM ~10:23 ICT, each with a PM source), `maxTriesFor` (MAX_TRIES plus the
  extras of the matching id and kind), and the tryGuard rewrite that uses the computed limit.
  Every changed runtime line belongs to the exception map or its use in the try count.
- Try counter across color versions: `countTries` filters rows only on time (>= RESTART_START),
  kind, picture id (via pictureKey), and excludes failed zero-cost rows. It has no version and no
  output-name filter. The printed "try t" of `doLine` in scripts/storytime-muse.mjs is a per
  color-version file suffix (t = first free `-line{t}` slot of the base `m{n}`) used for names
  only. The guard therefore counts every restart row of the picture and kind across color
  versions. Tests confirm it: `nutRows` builds rows with outputs `m1..m{n}` of the same kind and
  all count; the "another id" test counts 3 rows across m1/m2/m3 and refuses.
- The four required test facts hold in tests/storytime-muse-attempts.test.ts, adapted to the
  final caps of 5.11.15: nut line 3 rows allowed one more (cap 5), nut line 4 rows allowed and
  5 rows refused, nut color 3 rows allowed one more and 4 rows refused, another id at 3 rows
  refused in both kinds; `maxTriesFor` keeps every other id at MAX_TRIES (3).
